## Interface: 30300
## Title: COA Dungeon Run
## Notes: v0.23.0 - capture, display and CURATION. A dungeon route IS a sequence of pulls, so record the pulls: combat start and end are the markers, the path between them is sampled once a second out of combat, and both entrances are captured automatically. Records everything and filters nothing - judgement happens offline against the whole set. Also records the instance identity and DIFFICULTY at arrival, which bosses the route ENGAGED (never a roster, never a fraction), and who killed you at a terminal stop - read from the client's own DeathRecap rather than a second combat-log listener. The map draws a run back onto the client's own tiles and never learns a dungeon; point facts live on the MAP as a tooltip; the companion is the CURATION pane - load, rename, comment, delete, filter by kind, and slice by TIME with an envelope, a window, play and skip. Curation only ever changes what you SEE: nothing it does touches the record. Also a CUSTOM PIN: where the client emits no event, the player is the sensor - /dr pin drops a point and promotion gives it meaning later. The map now holds LAYERS rather than a run - a run slot and a route slot, loaded independently - because authoring a route means looking at the evidence it came from. And PROMOTION is the third surface: select a node, mint a beacon into a route or a personal note onto your own plane - place carries over, the event does not, and the meaning is edited in afterwards. And a prototype DRIVER consumes them: arm a route in its own dungeon, scan for the current stage only, say when you reach it, advance - built before the behaviours are defined because a consumer is how they declare themselves. The map ZOOMS and PANS, 1x to 4x, anchored on the view centre rather than the cursor - because the cursor is also the pen, and drawing tools are unusable on the coarser maps where a 5-yard radius is under two pixels. Its controls are a widget of their own: an increment toggle that cycles 125/150/200 per click, a pan pad that moves a quarter view per press, recentre and reset - and mouse-wheel zoom and right-click panning are TICKS that default OFF, because the wheel belongs to the world camera and right-drag to camera-look, and an addon should not take either without being asked. /dr
